      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a badger character. Draw this exact badger as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the long round grey furry body with its dark underside, seen from the side as in image 1, without head, legs or tail; its front end, normally under the head, rounded.\n2. the head: the black-and-white striped head with its two small rounded ears and black nose, facing left and a little down as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the nose and the rosy cheek; its neck end rounded.\n3. one front leg: the near front leg, short and dark with little claws, as in image 1, with a rounded shoulder at the top.\n4. one back leg: the near back leg, as in image 1, with a rounded hip at the top.\n5. the tail: the short fluffy grey tail, with a rounded base.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
